occupationalSummary:
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoBodyText&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 102%; margin: 12.55pt 12.8pt 0.0001pt 0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(51, 64, 70, 1)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px; letter-spacing: -0.4px&quot;&gt;This occupation is found in any sector or organisation that uses data research, machine learning (ML) computer algorithms and embed Artificial Intelligence (AI) computer models within its business including industries such as Government departments, agriculture and animal care, accommodation and food, education, public health, health and social care, financial, legal and other professional services, engineering, technology, manufacturing, retail, sales and marketing, the arts, creative media, journalism and media production transport and recreation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoBodyText&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 102%; margin: 12.55pt 12.8pt 0.0001pt 0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(51, 64, 70, 1)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px; letter-spacing: -0.4px&quot;&gt;The broad purpose of the occupation is to discover, devise validate, and enhance AI solutions to add value to the business or customers by developing the AI models to increase productivity through automation and increase business competitiveness, they drive industry advancements in AI to support, upscale and enhance human decision-making with the use of trained AI models.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoBodyText&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 102%; margin: 12.55pt 12.8pt 0.0001pt 0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(51, 64, 70, 1)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px; letter-spacing: -0.4px&quot;&gt;On qualification AI technologists can lead, support and carry out applied research and conduct horizon scanning, monitoring the present and future trends, to predict and create innovative impactful data-driven AI solutions and new AI projects. They work in often dynamic environments, but within the constraints of a specific business context and company strategies such as to create, support or replace human decision making and tasks. They develop robust, safe, and secure AI solutions using large datasets, computer vision, natural language processing, algorithms, or AI-driven systems. These technologies enhance precision, reduce human workload, and enable strategic automation - allowing people to focus on tasks where human insight adds the greatest value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoBodyText&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 102%; margin: 12.55pt 12.8pt 0.0001pt 0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(51, 64, 70, 1)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px; letter-spacing: -0.4px&quot;&gt;AI technologists champion and adopt the uses of computational machine learning (ML) and AI and its applications within their organisation, to assure the business investment in developing and improving AI solutions including AI products, tools, systems and operational infrastructure. They consider and embed into their AI solutions, AI safety measures that are informed by known potential or predicted risks or threats by assessment. Applying current legislation, regulations, data &amp;amp; AI frameworks and ethical best practice, to ensure transparency, explainability, fairness, and accountability - while recognising psychological, societal, and cultural factors that influence bias, trust, and risk in AI systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoBodyText&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 102%; margin: 12.55pt 12.8pt 0.0001pt 0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(51, 64, 70, 1)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px; letter-spacing: -0.4px&quot;&gt;In their daily work, an employee in this occupation interacts with a broad spectrum of people and collaborates with, and provides technical authority and insight to, a diverse business community of Clients, Customers, Senior Leaders, Data Scientists, ML Engineers, Data Engineers, AI Automation Engineers, Statisticians, Analysts, Research and Development Scientists.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoBodyText&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 102%; margin: 12.55pt 12.8pt 0.0001pt 0&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgba(51, 64, 70, 1)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14.6667px; letter-spacing: -0.4px&quot;&gt;They typically interact internally by business partnering, or externally with other organisations, such as local and international governments, businesses, policy regulators, academic research scientists and non-technical audiences to plan, implement, support and review AI strategies, policies and solutions. They work independently and collaboratively, they typically report to Heads of AI, Heads of Data, Chief AI Architects, Company Directors, AI Product Managers and senior decision makers within the organisation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
